IMPORT prelude

-- Policies of Assurance Act 1867 (Singapore) -- assigning a life insurance policy: who may sue the insurer in their own name
-- (s 1), equitable defences (s 2), written notice to the insurer and the priority and payment rules that hang on it (s 3), the
-- insurer's duty to print its address for notices on every policy (s 4), the form of an assignment (s 5 and the Schedule), the
-- insurer's acknowledgment of a notice (s 6), and the definitions (s 7). That is every operative section of the Act.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PAA1867.txt. The deposit says the edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". Its Legislative
-- History lists only the English Act (30 & 31 Vict., c. 144, commencement 20 August 1867), its application in Singapore from
-- 12 November 1993 under the Application of English Law Act 1993 (except section 8), and the 1994 Revised Edition (Chapter 392,
-- operation 20 May 1994). No amending Act is annotated.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0037 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. Not encoded: s 8 (short title); the Stamp Duties Act consequences of an assignment not "duly stamped"
-- (s 5); and the First Schedule exceptions and amendments under the Application of English Law Act 1993, which the Legislative
-- History mentions but which were not retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions (the skill was not loaded in this
-- session; the conventions of the finished naive rows were followed). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass,
-- no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Policies of Assurance Act 1867 -- assignment of life policies`

§§ `7 -- interpretation`

-- s 7: "policy of life assurance" or "policy" means "any instrument by which the payment of moneys by or out of the funds of an
-- assurance company, on the happening of any contingency depending on the duration of human life, is assured or secured";
-- "assurance company" means "every corporation, association, society, or company now or hereafter carrying on the business of
-- assuring lives, or survivorships, either alone or in conjunction with any other object or objects".
GIVEN `pays out of the funds of an assurance company` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `on a contingency depending on the duration of human life` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument is a policy of life assurance` IF
        `pays out of the funds of an assurance company`
    AND `on a contingency depending on the duration of human life`

-- Other objects do not take a body out of the definition: "either alone or in conjunction with any other object or objects".
GIVEN `carries on the business of assuring lives or survivorships` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `also pursues other objects` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is an assurance company` IF
    `carries on the business of assuring lives or survivorships`

§§ `Facts about an assignment, a notice and a claimant`

DECLARE Assignment HAS
    `made after the passing of this Act`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `by endorsement on the policy`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `by a separate instrument`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the words or to the effect of the Schedule`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `duly stamped`                                      IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Notice HAS
    `was given`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `in writing`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the date of the assignment`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the purport of the assignment`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `given to the assurance company liable`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `given at its principal place of business for the time being` IS A BOOLEAN
    `day received`                                      IS A NUMBER

DECLARE Claimant HAS
    `entitled by assignment`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitled by another derivative title`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `has the right in equity to receive the moneys`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `has the right to give the company an effectual discharge` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `3 -- notice of assignment`

-- s 3: no assignment made after the passing of this Act confers "any right to sue ... until a written notice of the date and
-- purport of such assignment has been given to the assurance company liable under such policy at its principal place of business
-- for the time being".
GIVEN `the notice` IS A Notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice satisfies s 3` IF
        `the notice`'s `was given`
    AND `the notice`'s `in writing`
    AND `the notice`'s `states the date of the assignment`
    AND `the notice`'s `states the purport of the assignment`
    AND `the notice`'s `given to the assurance company liable`
    AND `the notice`'s `given at its principal place of business for the time being`

-- The bar is on an "assignment"; s 1 also reaches a holder by "other derivative title", whom s 3 does not mention.
GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant, `the assignment` IS AN Assignment, `the notice` IS A Notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 bars the action` IF
        `the claimant`'s `entitled by assignment`
    AND `the assignment`'s `made after the passing of this Act`
    AND (NOT `the notice satisfies s 3` `the notice`)

§§ `1 -- the assignee may sue in its own name`

-- s 1: any person or corporation "entitled, by assignment or other derivative title, to a policy of life assurance, and possessing
-- at the time of action brought the right in equity to receive and the right to give an effectual discharge to the assurance
-- company liable under such policy for moneys thereby assured or secured, shall be at liberty to sue at law in the name of such
-- person or corporation to recover such moneys".
--
-- Whether the assignment was "duly stamped" (s 5) is not a condition in s 1 or s 3, so it is not read here. The Stamp Duties Act
-- may have its own consequence; that was not encoded.
GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant, `the assignment` IS AN Assignment, `the notice` IS A Notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant may sue in its own name` IF
        (   `the claimant`'s `entitled by assignment`
         OR `the claimant`'s `entitled by another derivative title`)
    AND `the claimant`'s `has the right in equity to receive the moneys`
    AND `the claimant`'s `has the right to give the company an effectual discharge`
    AND (NOT `s 3 bars the action` `the claimant` `the assignment` `the notice`)

§§ `3 -- priority between assignees`

-- s 3: "the date on which such notice was received shall regulate the priority of all claims under any assignment". The date of
-- the assignment itself plays no part. The Act does not say what happens when two notices arrive on the same day; on a tie
-- neither claim is given priority here (an encoding choice, not the text).
GIVEN `the first notice` IS A Notice, `the second notice` IS A Notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first claim has priority` IF
        `the notice satisfies s 3` `the first notice`
    AND (   (NOT `the notice satisfies s 3` `the second notice`)
         OR `the first notice`'s `day received` < `the second notice`'s `day received`)

§§ `3 -- payment before notice`

-- s 3: "a payment bona fide made in respect of any policy by any assurance company before the date on which such notice was received
-- shall be as valid against the assignee giving such notice as if this Act had not been passed". A payment ON the day of receipt
-- is not "before the date". INFERENCE: a notice that does not meet s 3 is treated as never received.
GIVEN `paid in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `day paid` IS A NUMBER, `the notice` IS A Notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment is valid against the assignee` IF
        `paid in good faith`
    AND (   (NOT `the notice satisfies s 3` `the notice`)
         OR `day paid` < `the notice`'s `day received`)

§§ `4 -- principal place of business on every policy`

-- s 4: "Every assurance company shall, on every policy issued by the company, specify its principal place of business at which
-- notices of assignment may be given in pursuance of this Act." No penalty or other consequence is stated in the Act.
GIVEN `policies issued` IS A NUMBER, `policies specifying the place` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company is in breach of s 4` IF
    `policies specifying the place` < `policies issued`

§§ `5 and the Schedule -- mode of assignment`

-- s 5: "Any such assignment may be made either by endorsement on the policy or by a separate instrument in the words or to the
-- effect set out in the Schedule, such endorsement or separate instrument being duly stamped." The Schedule: "I, A. B., ... do
-- hereby assign unto C. D., ... the [within] policy of assurance ...".
--
-- INFERENCE: the Schedule's "[within] policy" fits an endorsement, so the Schedule words are read as qualifying both modes. "May be
-- made" is permissive; whether an assignment in some other form is ineffective is not said, so this rule only answers whether
-- the assignment uses a mode s 5 provides.
GIVEN `the assignment` IS AN Assignment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assignment is in a s 5 mode` IF
        (   `the assignment`'s `by endorsement on the policy`
         OR `the assignment`'s `by a separate instrument`)
    AND `the assignment`'s `in the words or to the effect of the Schedule`
    AND `the assignment`'s `duly stamped`

§§ `6 -- acknowledgment of a notice`

-- s 6: every assurance company to whom notice was duly given "shall, upon the request in writing of any person by whom any such
-- notice was given or signed, or of his executors or administrators, deliver an acknowledgment in writing under the hand of the
-- manager, secretary, treasurer, or other principal officer". No time limit and no fee are stated.
DECLARE Requester IS ONE OF
    `the person who gave the notice`
    `the person who signed the notice`
    `an executor or administrator of that person`
    `a later assignee who gave no notice`

GIVEN `notice duly given` IS A BOOLEAN, `request in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `the requester` IS A Requester
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company must deliver an acknowledgment` IF
        `notice duly given`
    AND `request in writing`
    AND CONSIDER `the requester`
        WHEN `a later assignee who gave no notice` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 6: the acknowledgment, "if signed by a person being de jure or de facto the manager, secretary, treasurer, or other principal
-- officer of the assurance company ..., shall be conclusive evidence as against such company of it having duly received the
-- notice".
DECLARE Signatory IS ONE OF
    `the manager`
    `the secretary`
    `the treasurer`
    `another principal officer`
    `a clerk`

GIVEN `acknowledgment in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `the signatory` IS A Signatory, `holds that office de jure or de facto` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the acknowledgment is conclusive against the company` IF
        `acknowledgment in writing`
    AND `holds that office de jure or de facto`
    AND CONSIDER `the signatory`
        WHEN `a clerk` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `2 -- equitable defences`

-- s 2: "In any action on a policy of life assurance, a defence on equitable grounds, or a reply to such defence on similar grounds,
-- may be respectively pleaded and relied upon in the same manner and to the same extent as in any other personal action." Outside
-- an action on a life policy s 2 says nothing; FALSE means only that.
GIVEN `the action is on a policy of life assurance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2 lets an equitable defence or reply be pleaded` IF
    `the action is on a policy of life assurance`
